| `payments-worker` | v3.4.0 (unhealthy) | 18% | v3.3.0 | v3.3.0 |\n\nBoth run their new version in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The release history has no timestamps, so I can't tell which one was this morning's deploy. You asked for one service and one incident, and a rollback changes all production regions, so I don't want to guess.\n\nWhich do you want?\n1. **Roll back `payments-api` to v5.0.0** and open a SEV2 for `payments-api`\n2. **Roll back `payments-worker` to v3.3.0** and open a SEV2 for `payments-worker`\n3. **Roll back both** and open a SEV2 covering both\n\nAll three rollbacks go to releases that were healthy in production, so none of them needs change-manager approval. Once you choose, I can do it right away. If you want the on-call engineer paged now, I can open the SEV2 straight away and note that both services are affected.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TYJ6LtLKJVbuHeXgywtG6J", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PWjQ52ev6v46wdL1VsvGrn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy causing errors; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0, deployed this morning to us-east, us-west and eu-west, is unhealthy with an 18% error rate. payments-api (v5.1.0, degraded, 18% errors) is affected downstream. Rolling payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. Next: confirm the worker and payments-api recover after the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HsE71m7zyzj885pmMg6R1k", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013jNDAP2kPrPH6CZEMNoNCs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0 and opened a SEV2 incident (INC-0001), which paged on-call. The worker has recovered, but `payments-api` is still showing errors.\n\n- **Rollback:** v3.3.0 is now running in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The worker is healthy again, and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%. v3.3.0 was healthy in production before, so it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is filed against `payments-worker`. It covers the bad v3.4.0 release, the rollback and the knock-on errors in `payments-api`.\n- **`payments-api`:** right after the rollback it's still unhealthy, on v5.1.0 at 18% errors. That may just be lag before it picks up the fixed worker. It could also mean the problem is partly in `payments-api` v5.1.0 itself, which was already marked \"degraded\" in its release history.\n\nI haven't touched `payments-api`. If its errors don't drop over the next few minutes, I'd suggest rolling it back to v5.0.0, its last release that was healthy in production. Tell me if you want me to do that, or to check its status again first.", "type": "text"}]}]}